Enter python worked_example.py and press
Enter.

207
00:13:46,148 --> 00:13:50,305
The script runs the same calculations and
writes the case table, frame

208
00:13:50,339 --> 00:13:55,320
arrays and figures. In the file browser,
open the case table, then the

209
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:57,863
paired plot, then the uncertainty plot.

210
00:13:58,977 --> 00:14:01,508
These are files produced by the executed
script.

211
00:14:02,112 --> 00:14:06,141
The assertions verify that the frame
residuals reproduce the intended

212
00:14:06,222 --> 00:14:10,611
root-mean-square errors, that the exact
calculation contains thirty-two

213
00:14:10,681 --> 00:14:14,744
sign assignments, and that SciPy matches the
explicit enumeration.

214
00:14:15,441 --> 00:14:20,085
To adapt the example, replace the synthetic
scores with results from your

215
00:14:20,154 --> 00:14:24,508
protected evaluation. Retain the independent
case identifiers and

216
00:14:24,601 --> 00:14:27,260
reconsider the resampling and sign-swap
assumptions.

217
00:14:27,771 --> 00:14:30,615
Before running, predict the sign of the mean
difference.

218
00:14:31,219 --> 00:14:33,703
Afterwards, inspect each case and the mean.

219
00:14:34,307 --> 00:14:39,277
A fixed seed makes the calculation
repeatable; it does not repair a leaking

220
00:14:39,335 --> 00:14:44,501
split or create independence. The editor,
terminal and output files make

221
00:14:44,524 --> 00:14:48,379
the arithmetic transparent. Your
experimental design determines what the

222
00:14:48,437 --> 00:14:50,340
output can tell you.

223
00:14:50,958 --> 00:14:54,766
Return to our opening question: should the
neural model replace the simpler

224
00:14:54,824 --> 00:14:58,899
model for predicting the elongation of a
metal bar in a tensile test?

225
00:14:59,712 --> 00:15:04,391
In this teaching example, the candidate
reduces mean case-level error from

226
00:15:04,507 --> 00:15:09,070
0.148 to 0.133, an improvement of

227
00:15:09,139 --> 00:15:12,158
about ten percent, and it improves all five
cases.

228
00:15:12,762 --> 00:15:15,757
That is a promising effect within these
synthetic inputs.

229
00:15:16,454 --> 00:15:21,016
The illustrative paired bootstrap interval
